  title        = {How AI Is Rewiring Smart Homes and Personal Computing},
  abstract    = {As smart speakers, TVs, wearables, and appliances fill our homes, AI is turning them into a distributed, intelligent system that learns patterns, predicts needs, and adapts living spaces in real time. By combining data from microphones, Wi-Fi, BLE, mmWave, and other sensors, AI can localize users, infer context, and coordinate multiple devices to act together — locking screens when you walk away, automating lighting and HVAC, or sending wellness alerts. Advances in on-device processing, federated learning, and Matter-based interoperability make these systems private, scalable, and responsive, pushing computing toward a future of seamless, ambient intelligence.},
